WEBVTT

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.900
Good morning!

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.050
Good morning, Shizu.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:18.740
Good morning.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.430
Good morning.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.080
I'm so cold!

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.420
But it's nice and warm!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.050
Hang in there, sis.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.300
You're all here.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.420
Let's go.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.760
Yes ma'am!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:25.330
<b>Episode 3
Contact</b>

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.300
So that's where the prefectural 
tournament is held, huh?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.290
This takes me back.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.790
I'm so nervous!

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.680
Don't worry, sis.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.920
We've all gotten pretty good 
at playing against Harue.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.240
You really have.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.430
You're probably close in skill to
my old teammates by now.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.680
But...

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.800
you guys don't have an 
Akado playing for you!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.200
How obnoxious.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.330
There are so many people here.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.570
Are we playing them all?

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.940
Nara has a lot less than 
the other prefectures.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.690
Our neighbors in Osaka are

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.410
divided into north and south,

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.310
and it's still a really crowded scene.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.460
Hey look, it's the tournament schedule!

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.920
So, where's Achiga?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.930
<b>Bansei 

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.930
Don't tell me we're playing...

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.310
Bansei, right off the bat?

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.480
First player, 3rd Year
Kobashiri Yae

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.640
Second player, 3rd Year
Maruse Noriko

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.850
Third player, 3rd Year
Kimura Hina

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.060
Fourth player, 3rd Year
Ueda Ryouko

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.310
Fifth player, 2nd Year
Tatsumi Yuka

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.440
Good luck!

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.350
Ako.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.990
It doesn't matter.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.580
We would have had to play 
them sooner or later.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:50.870
That's right.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.050
We'd definitely have to play them,

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.470
if we're going to the nationals.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.290
<i>That's right!</i>

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.460
<i>We can't let them</i>

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.680
<i>intimidate us here if we're 
going to the nationals!</i>

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.180
<i>Steel yourself...</i>

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.550
<i>We're going to see Nodoka!</i>

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.300
All right!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.240
Let's beat Bansei!

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.770
Which high school will win 
a ticket to the nationals?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.620
With their nine year winning 
streak, will Bansei High School

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.110
make it ten straight?

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:20.530
Or does a new challenger 
lie in wait for them?

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.910
For the first round match in the 
prefectural tournament,

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.530
Bansei will be playing Aramaki, 
Achiga, and Kasugano.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.560
Let the first round match of the 
prefectural tournament begin!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.580
Senpai!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.840
Fight!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.550
<i>A three sided wait, which includes a dora...</i>

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.950
<i>I'll show you...</i>

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:12.950
Riichi!

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.960
<i>...how royalty plays!</i>

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:21.750
Tsumo.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.720
Seven Dora. That's 8000 from all.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.560
Matsumi Kuro, from Achiga Girls' Academy,

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.930
in the first hand of the match

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.390
Baiman - A hand of 8-10 han worth 24000
 points as dealer, or 16000 otherwise.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.390
wins with a Seven Dora Tsumo, a dealer baiman.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.890
Senpai?

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.210
Ron.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.290
Tsumo!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:51.680
Ron.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.130
It's the last hand of the fifth player's match,

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.670
with Achiga holding the lead.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.910
Matsumi Kuro created an 
overwhelming lead in the first player's match,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.170
and her teammates have done 
a good job protecting it.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.140
Bansei's players are doing 
their best to catch up, but...

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.100
Ron!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.760
That'll be 2,600 points.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.600
That settles it!

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.320
Achiga has cleared the first round match.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.610
Bansei will not get a
10th consecutive win!

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.240
Th-this can't be...

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.860
Let's just keep going like this,
 until we're the best!

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:40.490
But of course!

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.710
Let's go to the nationals!

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.000
Where Nodoka is waiting for us!

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:08.110
Congratulations to Achiga Girl's Academy's
 Mahjong Club for making it to Nationals

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.710
Hmm... it feels like we 
made it, for now at least.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:15.640
Yeah, huh?

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:16.950
It wasn't easy, though.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.620
Did you see the paper?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.020
I saw it on the internet.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.170
The winning school for 
Nagano prefecture is...

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:29.670
Kiyosumi!

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:36.930
<b>Kiyosumi High's Debut!</b>

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.790
That's Nodoka's school!

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.590
I knew she'd make it through!

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.930
I've never heard of that 
school before, though.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.220
Oh?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.940
I mean, talking about 
Nagano's famous schools,

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.520
it would be Kazekoshi or something.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.960
The team that made it to 
Nationals last year

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.900
is supposed to be really strong, too.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.860
But now we can finally meet 
her at the nationals!

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.530
Yeah.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.730
That reminds me... 
where's Yuu-nee and Arata-san?

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.990
Arata-chan went shopping with Akado-sensei.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.400
And my sis got stormed by her classmates

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.500
because they saw her on TV.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.190
You're not going to help her?

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.620
Being in the middle of a
crowd is nice and warm.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.180
I'm sure she's happy.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.520
I hope you're right.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.760
Everybody's here, right?

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.260
Speak of the devil.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.500
All right!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.800
I know this is sudden,

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.060
but let's talks about the road to Nationals.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.020
Yeah!

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:28.270
Training Camp?

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.880
Hmm, it's not quite camp,

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.070
but more like away-matches, every weekend.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:33.910
Every weekend?!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.860
You know, back when I
 went to the nationals,

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.450
prefectural representatives were not
allowed to play practice matches.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.410
Not even against grade schoolers?!

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.890
Yup. But now, the rules have changed.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.560
You can play matches,

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.840
but not against other 
prefectural representatives.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.130
Which means that

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.920
you're allowed to face off 
against any prefecture's

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.400
school that came in second place.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.510
We've got seven weekends 
until the nationals.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.260
We're going to spend 
that time travelling,

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.770
defeating all the second 
ranking schools!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.230
Wow.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.150
Can we really do that?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.660
Since we got our ticket to Nationals,

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.050
the Mahjong Support 
Club has been revived,

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.390
and our club funds have grown.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.620
We should have enough 
to cover our expenses,

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.410
so it just depends on getting

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.040
permission from your parents.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.560
I'm sure my parents 
would be fine with it.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.450
Mine, too.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.190
Huh?

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.170
I guess.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.140
All right!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.040
Then we just have to decide which

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.750
school we're going up against 
and ask for a-

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:31.670
Nagano.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.510
I want to go up against 
Nagano's number two.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.670
Nagano?

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.800
That's fine...

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.180
I'll try to set that up first then.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.180
Nagano

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.680
<i>This school, huh.</i>

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.770
It's the mountains!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:53.980
That's great!

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.360
We're in the mountains, too...

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.350
<i>Before the prefectural tournament,</i>

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:03.120
<i>I thought your guys' dreams 
would never come true.</i>

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.220
<i>Not because of us...</i>

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.610
<i>I knew we had a chance against Bansei.</i>

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:12.630
<i>I simply did not see Nodoka's 
high school making it through.</i>

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:18.750
<i>I mean I watched Nagano's team 
in last year's tournament...</i>

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.780
Wow...

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.410
This is like a reception hall.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.660
This is Nagano's second best school.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.420
This way, please.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:49.990
Please go in.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.510
We've been waiting for you.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.510
Ryuumonbuchi High School
Ryuumonbuchi Touka

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.760
So these guys are playing for Nara?

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.760
Ryuumonbuchi High School
Inoue Jun

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.510
You shouldn't call them "these guys."

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.510
Ryuumonbuchi High School
Kunihiro Hajime

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.390
Ryuumonbuchi High School
Sawamura Tomoki

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.390
Nice to meet you.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.540
<i>This is...</i>

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.200
Ryuumonbuchi High School
Amae Koromo

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.490
Your trip must have been quite long.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.620
<i>This is the...</i>

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.200
<i>school that came in second in Nagano,</i>

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.920
<i>Ryuumonbuchi High!</i>

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.380
Yay! Looks like Koromo won again!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.770
I can't win.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.110
This is the third time 
she's won with the very last tile!

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.020
It's strange.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.990
<i>That's Ryuumonbuchi's Amae Koromo.</i>

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.780
<i>Just like I thought, 
she's a national-class monster.</i>

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.830
<i>If she keeps going, 
she'll end up like I was.</i>

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.780
<i>Maybe I should stop her now.</i>

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:06.930
Amae-san!

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.100
You are really, really good!

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.470
So Nodoka, I mean,

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.960
Kiyosumi really beat you?

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:18.230
No, it wasn't Nonoka who beat Koromo.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.960
It was their rinshan user.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:20.880
[Rinshan kaihou - winning with the extra
 tile drawn when you declare a kan]

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.880
And you know, Koromo can't

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.350
even use half her power right now.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.600
The moon isn't full and it's evening.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.330
Rinshan user?

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:30.350
The moon?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.510
I have no idea what you're talking about,

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.360
but please play me again!

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.890
Are you sure?

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:38.600
Yes!

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.050
I want to play, too.

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.990
You're going to play with Koromo, too?

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.690
Let's join, too.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:52.200
Me, too.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.530
I guess then...

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.500
We'll play, too.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:58.940
Me, too.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:04.020
I will start preparing the evening meal.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.390
Let the games begin!

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.800
Let's play!

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.240
I won't lose again!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.690
Huh.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.690
In some respects, she's stronger than me.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.910
Let's play!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.850
Ryuumonbuchi   Sensui Girls'   Sangamaki
Tatsuike   Sunpu   Katasenogi   Shinma Girls'

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.230
All right!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.350
You beat all the teams, 
except Ryuumonbuchi.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.230
Looking good.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:42.150
But none of us were able 
to beat that one player

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.890
from North Osaka's Sangamaki.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.410
Well...

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.720
Arakawa Kei came in second 
in the individual tournament

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.270
in last year's nationals.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:51.030
If you all could beat her,

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.560
then winning the nationals 
would be a piece of cake.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.460
If you flip that statement, 
it means that since

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.100
we can't beat her, 
we can't win the nationals.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.190
Team power.

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:02.960
The fact that Sangamaki 
is second in North Osaka

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.200
means that their team's power

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.680
is lower than Senriyama's.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:06.530
That is to say...

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:13.220
Improve Team power => Training camp!

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.990
We should also use our 
team's power to win.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:13.600
Which is why starting the day after tomorrow,
 for summer break,

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.740
we're going to improve all of your skills
at a 10 day training camp.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:19.720
After that, you'll get a
 few days rest at home.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.750
Then, we're off to the
 home of the nationals...

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.050
<b>Win the Nationals!</b>

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.050
Tokyo!

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.560
Welcome, Members of the 
Achiga Girls' Mahjong Club

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.960
<b>Women</b>

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:35.740
Win the Nationals!

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.520
Take care!

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:37.290
Good luck!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.750
Good luck!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:44.970
Ako.

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:48.630
Hatsuse!

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.630
What is it?

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:56.340
Did your callouses get even bigger?

00:15:56.340 --> 00:16:01.060
Actually, I think they're okay now.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.770
You guys are even stronger

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.070
than at the prefectural tournament.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:08.230
So you could take Nationals.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.070
Of course.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.700
We've got something to take 
care of at Nationals!

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.700
We're about to leave.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.260
Okay!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.370
Good luck, Ako!

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:23.750
You, too!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:24.840
Yeah.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.540
I'm going to win next year!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.300
All right!

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.640
Ako-chan! Everyone!

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.000
We can't let them down.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:42.140
Yes.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.860
Break time!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.990
It's pretty tiring to sit 
in the car for so long.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.410
How much longer until Tokyo?

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.100
About three more hours.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.600
That's so far!

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.770
What about Yuu-nee?

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.200
She's still asleep.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.640
We're going to the store. 
You guys need anything?

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:10.200
Just something to drink.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.090
All right.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.000
Then you can go walk around.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.010
Okay.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:22.860
It's so hot!

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.200
It's good that it's a 
little overcast, though.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.550
If the sun was out, it would be even hotter!

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.400
We'd die!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.150
Look.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:33.260
There's some girl in a uniform.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.150
Kind of like us.

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:46.570
Whoa, she fell over!

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.710
Heat stroke?

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.460
Are you all right?

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:52.680
Toki,

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.800
are you okay?

00:17:56.400 --> 00:18:00.270
Ryuuka, sorry for being a bother again.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:17.540
This is good.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.070
Are you feeling better?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.240
Sorry to cause a scene.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.860
I'm a bit sickly.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.500
Oh, stop talking like that.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:27.960
That reminds me.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.650
Why are you wearing 
your school uniforms?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:32.750
Because we're participating in 
an event for a school club.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.630
Could it be...

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.280
Toki!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.070
The bus is about to leave!

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:42.610
Please hurry, senpai.

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:43.830
We've got to go.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.230
It was fun.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.200
Yeah.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.280
The bus is about to leave!

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.500
Eguchi-senpai, can you stop 
being so embarrassing?

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.000
Here you are!

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:56.880
Akado-san!

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.400
Huh?

00:18:57.770 --> 00:19:00.090
That's Senriyama.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.160
Senriyama?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:04.450
They've got four buses over there,

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.320
all full of kids with that uniform.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:08.790
They're ranked second  in the country.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.540
The fourth seed in the 
inter-high tournament:

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.930
Senriyama Girls' High!

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:16.300
The strongest school in the Kansai region!

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:34.810
I've booked three twin rooms like these.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.710
Wow, this is so luxurious!

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:37.850
Everyone, pick your rooms

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.320
and let's get some rest.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.890
We finally made it to Tokyo.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.310
To the nationals.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:48.200
Yeah.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.460
Are you going to meet with Nodoka?

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:53.310
No. If she's not coming,

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.710
I'm not going to go either.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:59.200
Anyway, I just want to face 
off against Kiyosumi.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.440
All right, Arata, take our place in the lottery.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.070
Okay.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.610
Go get 'em!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.100
Fight, Arata-chan!

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:23.280
Good luck!

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:26.280
I'm just drawing our lot, geez.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:27.880
That reminds me.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:30.260
How come Arata-chan is the captain?

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.770
Does that upset you, 
as the only third year in the club?

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:37.310
No. I could never get in front
 of a crowd and draw a lot,

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:38.990
so I'm glad I don't have to do it.

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:40.650
Well, there's your answer.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:43.850
Arata's the most composed 
girl on this team.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.930
That makes sense.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:54.060
So what if you run into 
Nodoka by accident?

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.280
Then we'll have to just 
deal with it.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.320
It might really happen...

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.440
Well, I think we all want to 
meet her as soon as possible!

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:13.330
W-what?

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.840
That uniform...

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.590
It's Kiyosumi!

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:40.970
No, it wasn't Nonoka who beat Koromo.

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:42.860
It was their rinshan user.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.420
<i>They're the same year.</i>

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.320
<i>What did she say her name was?</i>

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.370
<i>I think it was... Saki.</i>

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.880
<i>Miyanaga Saki!</i>

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:55.870
That's...

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:59.030
That's the girl I have to beat!

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:36.470
In the 21st century,

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.560
the number of mahjong players around

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:41.790
the world is in the hundreds of millions,

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:44.300
and the professional players 
have an avid following.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.110
Even at the high school level,

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:49.800
a large-scale national tournament 
is held every year.

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:54.120
That's where the high 
school players compete

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:57.370
in order to make it into the 
league of professionals.

00:23:58.130 --> 00:24:03.210
This is the path of the girls 
who were aiming for the top.

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:19.870
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:09.510
Tokyo! Hey, where should we go?

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:11.440
You can't forget about the nationals!

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:12.860
But I do want to go to Harajuku...

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:13.930
I want to go to Akiba!

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:16.230
I want to look at Da-pans at Nogami.

00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:17.250
That sounds like a great idea!

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:18.980
Sounds good, but what is that?

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:25.000
<b>Please watch us again!</b>
